allest multiple of 7 greater than or equal to 100:**\n   - To find the smallest multiple of 7 that is at least 100, we divide 100 by 7 and round up to the nearest whole number.\n   - \\( \\frac{100}{7} \\approx 14.2857 \\)\n   - Rounding up, we get 15.\n   - Therefore, the smallest multiple of 7 in this range is \\( 7 \\times 15 = 105 \\).\n\n2. **Identify the largest multiple of 7 less than or equal to 200:**\n   - To find the largest multiple of 7 that is at most 200, we divide 200 by 7 and round down to the nearest whole number.\n   - \\( \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.5714 \\)\n   - Rounding down, we get 28.\n   - Therefore, the largest multiple of 7 in this range is \\( 7 \\times 28 = 196 \\).\n\n3. **Determine the sequence and its properties:**\n   - The multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\( a = 105 \\), common difference \\( d = 7 \\), and the last term \\( l = 196 \\).\n   - The number of terms \\( n \\) in this sequence can be found using the formula for the \\( n \\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence: \\( a_n = a + (n-1)d \\).\n   - Setting \\( a_n = 196 \\):\n     \\[\n     196 = 105 + (n-1) \\cdot 7\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\( n \\):\n     \\[\n     196 - 105 = (n-1) \\cdot 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     91 = (n-1) \\cdot 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     n-1 = 13\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     n = 14\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the sum of the arithmetic sequence:**\n   - The sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     S_n = \\frac{n}{2} \\left( a + l \\right)\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the known values:\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = \\frac{14}{2} \\left( 105 + 196 \\right)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 7 \\times 301\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 2107\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2107}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
